{"title":"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The table shows the ages of all the children in the Gauss Choir. How many of the children are older than 7?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(add table: age 6 -&gt; 8 children, age 7 -&gt; 10 children, age 8 -&gt; 7 children, age 9 -&gt; 2 children)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In total, Pierre has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82eb3ef8c7329a4d1970a90c67cf6ad5e7e199f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times \\$1 + 1 \\times \\$2 + 2 \\times \\$5 + 4 \\times$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"240\" height=\"17\" />10<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f356a1e6247c7c5a16518b38b6d1dd90ae14cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\$2 + \\$2 + \\$10 + \\$40 = \\$4 + \\$50 = \\$54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"322\" height=\"17\" /> from the coins and dollar bills that he has.\n</p><p>If he splits this equally among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> people, each person must get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8aeb4a929f9362ef290aa0f76f16c443a74710c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\$54}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c847364af38a7e9dca648584ea992ec70aae749b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, each person gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b0a1d9703aefd28188ffa219d3865b99e6c1d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\$54}{9} = \\boxed{\\$6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"40\" /> \n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC\">2021 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B